    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0280" n="200" xml:id="pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/1145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-28T14:00:00-05:00">November 28, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Your 39, 40, 41, 42, of November 26, your 44 of November 27 and your No. 45
                    of November 28.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d187-f1"/> Department approves of texts as
                    telegraphed on the clear understanding that such approval does not prejudice its
                    attitude at the final conference, when figures are under discussion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
